{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut","id":1430805,"title":"Reasonably detailed descriptions of Juggernaut?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-02T16:15:57-08:00","id":1430805,"title":"Reasonably detailed descriptions of Juggernaut?","content":"My players are on their way to Thorns, presumably with the intent of challenging the Seven-Degreed Physician of Black Maladies. Are there any really good descriptions of Juggernaut, beyond &quot;giant animated corpse with a castle built on it?&quot; Is it humanoid, or otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T00:13:09-08:00","id":1430836,"title":"","content":"I think the most comprehensive descriptions make it out to be pretty humanoid, like it has what was described as &quot;hands&quot; it's on all fours, but it's also crippled so it's possible it's just on its hands and knees. It's also a rotting corpse, so I imagine a lot of decayed flesh attached to bones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T00:20:02-08:00","id":1430837,"title":"","content":"Juggernaut has been around since 1e, and has accumulated quite a bit of lore.<br /> <br /> Yes, Juggernaut is humanoid. It can't walk or stand upright, instead dragging itself along on its belly with its arms (leaving it's back free to support the Mask's fortress).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T01:54:52-08:00","id":1430851,"title":"","content":"3E core:<br /> <br /> &quot;Now a black miasma boils up around the city, obscuring the gray fields, the leafless trees, and the grotesque foot-hills that rise, bloated and repellent, outside her walls. But they are not hills. These ragged slopes are mounds of rotten flesh; that promontory an elbow, those gorges the gaps between fingers like fallen spires. Thorns is now a shadowland, its panorama dominated by the vast and terrible undead giant called Juggernaut which slumps supine outside the city gates, from between whose shoulders rises the osseous castle of the Mask of Winters. [...]<br /> <br /> &quot;Juggernaut was a fearsome behemoth slain in the forgotten epochs of the First Age\u2014a terror with fists the size of hills, the bulk of its flesh like a city wrought in muscle and sinew. The Deathlord found the behemoth\u2019s ancient corpse and enslaved it through unimaginably potent sorceries, raised his citadel upon its rotting back, then set it crawling toward the city.&quot;<br /> <br /> 1E Abyssals<br /> <br /> There's a Chapter Fiction on page 263 that describes a massive belly filled with maggots. There aren't any stand-out passages, but it's evocative.<br /> <br /> 2E's MoEP Abyssal says:<br /> <br /> &quot;The great undead monstrosity would be one mile tall if it stood upright. Currently, it crawls about ponderously on its hands and knees. Its master placed towers of basalt and ebony on its back to serve as a command center.&quot;<br /> <br /> But the gold can be found in Compass: Scavenger Lands. There's a full stat block and illustration on page 154, which is as detailed as you're going to get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-06-2021, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T21:37:13-08:00","id":1430955,"title":"","content":"IIRC in one of those descriptions it's mentioned that it doesn't have a face; it's been long-since obliterated and I want to say there's further construction inside the opened skull though that might just be my own imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T23:33:35-08:00","id":1430958,"title":"","content":"Likewise, I think one or more mentions implied a &quot;big reveal&quot; that Juggernaught isn't the corpse of a dead behemoth that the Mask animated like a zombie, but rather the gravely wounded, but slowly regenerating body of a *living* behemoth that Mask uses Necromancy to keep at the city-sized-giant-equivalent of Incapacitated so that a legion of nemessaries can possess the necrotizing muscles and coordinate its movements. I.e., the ghosts make it crawl, the Mask's &quot;unfathomable necromancy&quot; is what keeps it from standing up.<br /> <br /> Or that could be headcanon I accidentally synthesized over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-04-2021, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T06:16:23-08:00","id":1430979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1430955#post1430955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC in one of those descriptions it's mentioned that it doesn't have a face; it's been long-since obliterated and I want to say there's further construction inside the opened skull though that might just be my own imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you did make it up it ought to be canon, because that's rad as hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T07:20:10-08:00","id":1430984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1430958#post1430958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, I think one or more mentions implied a &amp;quot;big reveal&amp;quot; that Juggernaught isn't the corpse of a dead behemoth that the Mask animated like a zombie, but rather the gravely wounded, but slowly regenerating body of a *living* behemoth that Mask uses Necromancy to keep at the city-sized-giant-equivalent of Incapacitated so that a legion of nemessaries can possess the necrotizing muscles and coordinate its movements. I.e., the ghosts make it crawl, the Mask's &amp;quot;unfathomable necromancy&amp;quot; is what keeps it from standing up.<br /> <br /> Or that could be headcanon I accidentally synthesized over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>No that's from Compass: Scavenger Lands with the write up.<br /> <br /> Also, Juggernaut is humanoid. Just huge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T07:02:57-08:00","id":1431287,"title":"","content":"...Wait, does it really say \u201csupine?\u201d<br /> <br /> ...Yep, \u201csupine.\u201d Either someone meant \u201cprone\u201d or Mask\u2019s castle is now a powder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T09:57:06-08:00","id":1431295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1431287#post1431287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Wait, does it really say \u201csupine?\u201d<br /> <br /> ...Yep, \u201csupine.\u201d Either someone meant \u201cprone\u201d or Mask\u2019s castle is now a powder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... so... I'm fighting a guy with a sledgehammer. They're facing me and swing the hammer into me making a smashing attack... that, somehow, knocks me prone. How? Wut? Surely it'd knock me on my ass (aka supine)? Latin is hard, apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T12:39:48-08:00","id":1431308,"title":"","content":"As best I understand, Juggernaut was introduced as a relatively straightforward dead giant whose corpse was animated by the most powerful necromancy. There was also a whole thing where its real value to the Mask of Winters was the maggots being cultivated within its flesh, that when ready would burst forth to be unleashed on somebody (I think originally the rival Deathlords).<br /> <br /> The Second Edition entry was the one that introduced the idea that Juggernaut wasn't properly dead, allowing for a prospect of functioning independently without the Mask. I recall some writers being critical of this change in a time towards Second Edition's end.<br /> <br /> I would expect there's a good prospect of Third Edition reverting to the original, if only to trim some fat from the concept.<br /> <br /> Heh, while I expect the description of lying supine was in error, I'm now suddenly imagining the citadel working like Tokyo-3, i.e. the buildings can rise through the flesh to stand inverted from the chest. It would be reminiscent of Mask's gimmick for turning around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T13:21:31-08:00","id":1431315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1431308#post1431308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, while I expect the description of lying supine was in error, I'm now suddenly imagining the citadel working like Tokyo-3, i.e. the buildings can rise through the flesh to stand inverted from the chest. It would be reminiscent of Mask's gimmick for turning around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this so much that hitting the &quot;like&quot; button isn't enough. This is canon now.<br /> <br /> As for the idea of Juggernaut being alive, Compass: Scavenger Lands says he's alive. Then Manual Abyssals, which literally references book and page number for Juggernaut's stats, turns round and says &quot;nah, it's dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, the Essence harvesting maggots have been the big thing since 1E. I'd be surpised if they didn't make a return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T13:53:50-08:00","id":1431321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1431308#post1431308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As best I understand, Juggernaut was introduced as a relatively straightforward dead giant whose corpse was animated by the most powerful necromancy. There was also a whole thing where its real value to the Mask of Winters was the maggots being cultivated within its flesh, that when ready would burst forth to be unleashed on somebody (I think originally the rival Deathlords).<br /> <br /> The Second Edition entry was the one that introduced the idea that Juggernaut wasn't properly dead, allowing for a prospect of functioning independently without the Mask. I recall some writers being critical of this change in a time towards Second Edition's end.<br /> <br /> I would expect there's a good prospect of Third Edition reverting to the original, if only to trim some fat from the concept.<br /> <br /> Heh, while I expect the description of lying supine was in error, I'm now suddenly imagining the citadel working like Tokyo-3, i.e. the buildings can rise through the flesh to stand inverted from the chest. It would be reminiscent of Mask's gimmick for turning around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would suggest that any parts involved in the &quot;Schrodinger's Juggernaut&quot; debate and what edition actually did what should probably give a good, long read of the chapter 7 fiction in page 263 of 1e Exalted: the Abyssals, for a bit of perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-06-2021, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T01:22:03-08:00","id":1431364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1431321#post1431321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest that any parts involved in the &quot;Schrodinger's Juggernaut&quot; debate and what edition actually did what should probably give a good, long read of the chapter 7 fiction in page 263 of 1e Exalted: the Abyssals, for a bit of perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>1E presentation is hella cool nuanced take on life and death, with a cool twist. Then 2E did the 2E thing. But yeah, you can see where Compass: Scavenger Lands comes from.<br /> <br /> 1E: &quot;Juggernaut is dead, like the Neverborn.&quot;<br /> 2E: &quot;Juggernaut is ALIVE!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T02:40:22-08:00","id":1431368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1431364#post1431364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1E presentation is hella cool nuanced take on life and death, with a cool twist. Then 2E did the 2E thing. But yeah, you can see where Compass: Scavenger Lands comes from.<br /> <br /> 1E: &quot;Juggernaut is dead, like the Neverborn.&quot;<br /> 2E: &quot;Juggernaut is ALIVE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 2E version, tried to work on a kernel of an idea - while completely forgetting to check the source so they get it right, as 2E frequently did - simplyfing/flanderizing in the proccess.<br /> As an aside, i think Juggernaut's stats had already been published in one of the late 1e books, but can't say for sure which one, so don't take my word for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T03:10:29-08:00","id":1431372,"title":"","content":"I quite like the idea that, like the neverborn, Juggernaut comes from an era when death was not a concept that existed, and so cannot truly die, only be destroyed (which is what happened to the neverborn. Destroyed, but not dead and so re-appeared in the underworld). So juggernaut has been &quot;mortally&quot; wounded by some badass solar of ancient times and slunk off to die, but can't because death isn't a thing that can happen to it. So it remains slain but not dead, hovering at that point with wounds too grievous to heal itself and that effectively render its body lifeless, but not dead.<br /> So along comes MoW and finds this paradox of a monster and finds that it is dead enough to use necromancy on. He binds it, builds a castle on it and turns it into a siege weapon, mobile fortress, terrifying-symbol-of-power and off he goes.<br /> Which leaves the tantalising option open of some solar PC coming along with insane healing charms and healing Juggernaut enough to bring it back from mostly-dead to partly-alive (tip of the hat to Miracle Max) and ending MoW's control over it. You could then see Juggernaut destroying the castle on its back and maye rolling over Masks army, a huge setback for MoW. But what happens after that, as Juggernaut regenerates to full health? Does the Ender-of-civilizations pick up where it left off an start rampaging around creation again? Will the players need to track it down and try and kill or bind it? Is it in fact a bigger threat than MoW ever was?<br /> All good storytelling material.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T03:28:15-08:00","id":1431377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1431368#post1431368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The 2E version, tried to work on a kernel of an idea - while completely forgetting to check the source so they get it right, as 2E frequently did - simplyfing/flanderizing in the proccess.<br /> As an aside, i think Juggernaut's stats had already been published in one of the late 1e books, but can't say for sure which one, so don't take my word for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not an expert in 1E. I played it since release, but I was a broke-ass teenager, and didn't pick up most of the 1E books until the 3E kickstarter. But lemme have a look...<br /> <br /> It's not in Creatures of the Wyld, or the Book of Bone and Ebony (which DOES have stats for necromantic warmachines, the maggots inside of Juggernaut, a reborn Juggernaut of the Second Age, and rules for making a Juggernaut-like creation), or Games of Divinity, or Abyssals, or the ST Companion, or the Player's Guide. I can't think where else to look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T05:09:12-08:00","id":1431386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1431377#post1431377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not an expert in 1E. I played it since release, but I was a broke-ass teenager, and didn't pick up most of the 1E books until the 3E kickstarter. But lemme have a look...<br /> <br /> It's not in Creatures of the Wyld, or the Book of Bone and Ebony (which DOES have stats for necromantic warmachines, the maggots inside of Juggernaut, a reborn Juggernaut of the Second Age, and rules for making a Juggernaut-like creation), or Games of Divinity, or Abyssals, or the ST Companion, or the Player's Guide. I can't think where else to look.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember for sure there being a 1E Essence 8 version of Juggernaut - because my first thought upon seeing the 2E version was <i>Whoever did this rewrite <u>definitely</u> did it with my &quot;<b>prime ribs for Han-Tha's apotheosis</b>&quot; comment in the WW forums in mind</i>....<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Who knows, i might be mangling bits from the Book of Bone and Ebony through faulty memory from too long without checking stuff. Probably that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-07-2021, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-07T07:00:28-08:00","id":1431396,"title":"","content":"Juggernaut of the Second Age is Essence 7, so an Essence 8 Juggernaut makes sense. I'll keep looking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T09:15:10-08:00","id":1431470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1430805-reasonably-detailed-descriptions-of-juggernaut?p=1431396#post1431396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Juggernaut of the Second Age is Essence 7, so an Essence 8 Juggernaut makes sense. I'll keep looking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Essence 7 <b><i>might </i></b>be a viable target for the &quot;munching for apotheosis&quot; tactic too. Considering i left the idea by the wayside since CoTD: Scavenger Lands came out, my mind be mixing things because the Vodak (possibly another target for Han-Tha munching) is Essence 8 is not out of the equation.<br /> Main matter is that Juggernaut being &quot;downgraded&quot; Ess6 - truth be told, neither version seem to have anything for which the change would affect much - definitely ganked by mad plans from back then.<br /> <br /> That and the fact &quot;Juggernaut of the Second Age&quot; looks anything <i><b>but </b></i>humanoid - or even vertebrate, for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-08-2021, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}